WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:01.589
The company or country is in

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:03.899
decline. You can try voice

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:05.309
or you can try exit.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:06.449
Voice is basically changing the

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:08.339
system from within, whereas

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:09.839
exit is leaving to create the new

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:10.319
system.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.269
In 2013, the serial entrepreneur

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:15.329
Balaji Srinivasan gave a widely

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.189
discussed talk at the tech incubator

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:19.439
Y Combinator on a paradigm

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:20.549
derived from the work of the

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:21.959
economist Albert O.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:22.889
Hirschman.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.749
There are two paths to reform, he

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:25.709
explained.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.719
To speak up and remake a system from

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:28.619
within.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.689
Or to leave and build something new

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:32.699
that might one day take its place.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.919
That latter concept of exit

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.209
is the framework through which

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.399
Silicon Valley solves problems,

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.719
and it captures the worldview of

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:41.999
Srinivasan, who venture capitalist

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.949
Marc Andreessen has said has the

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:45.959
highest output per minute of new

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:47.999
ideas of anybody I've ever

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.229
met in my life.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:51.359
In his new book, The Network State

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.219
How to Start a New Country,

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.019
Srinivasan makes the case for

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:56.999
exiting today's nation states as

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.219
they exist and migrating much,

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:01.289
though not all of our lives onto

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:02.159
the Internet.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.018
Ever improving digital tools give

00:01:04.019 --> 00:01:05.849
humans an unprecedented and

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:07.709
always accelerating ability to

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:09.659
create opt in, fully

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:11.489
voluntary communities where people

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:13.739
choose to meet, work,

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.719
live and love from existing

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:16.859
countries that are changing

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.599
themselves by attracting immigrants

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:19.919
with the promise of a better

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:21.119
standard of living.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.159
To blockchain communities that draw

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:25.199
participants by laying out clear cut

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.509
contractual rules, responsibilities

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:29.279
and obligations, Srinivasan

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:31.169
articulates a future

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:33.119
that is profoundly democratic and

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:35.129
consensual, thus liberating

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:36.599
us from a status quo in which

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.549
self-determination is usually

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:40.259
little more than a pipe dream.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:41.969
Srinivasan holds a Ph.D.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:43.229
in electrical engineering from

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:44.039
Stanford.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:45.749
He co-founded the genetic testing

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:47.699
firm Counsyl, and he served as

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.709
the first chief technology officer

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:51.359
of Coinbase, the popular

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.129
cryptocurrency exchange.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:54.689
He's been a fierce critic over the

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:56.789
years of the FDA, which might

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:58.739
account for his being shortlisted to

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:00.509
head up the agency under Donald

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:01.709
Trump.

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:03.629
What if this coronavirus is the

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:05.369
pandemic that public health people

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:07.229
have been warning about for years?

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:09.478
He tweeted in January 2020,

00:02:09.479 --> 00:02:11.669
as Vox and mainstream outlets

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:13.859
were busy attacking Silicon Valley

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.719
venture capitalists for taking

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.489
the crisis too seriously.

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:19.469
It would accelerate many preexisting

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:21.419
trends, he wrote: border closures,

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:23.849
nationalism, social isolation,

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:25.799
preppers, remote work, face

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:28.229
masks, distrust in governments.

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:30.359
Reason talked with Srinivasan about

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:32.249
the network state, the rise

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:34.379
of China as a tightly centralized

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.719
global power, why Peter Thiel

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:39.269
is part of the descending class,

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:41.039
and the future of freedom, both

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.330
online and off.

00:02:46.229 --> 00:02:47.039
Balaji. Thanks for talking to

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:47.969
Reason.

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:48.869
Good to be here.

